            <ArticleTitle>Mechanism(s) of calcium antagonists and ischemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>89-93</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An overview is provided of the mechanismen of action of the three main calcium antagonists: nifedipine, verapamil and diltiazem, in ischemic heart disease. The thesis is proposed that in individual cases with angina pectoris and ischemic heart disease different and differing actions must be expected with this type of pharmaco-therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
